    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0610" n="596" xml:id="pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1216M/2257</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bursley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Adviser on Political Relations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-11">February 11, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received February
                        13.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Larry</hi>: I refer to my letter of February
                    10th regarding the water matter.</p>
                <p>I have just found time to read the latest batch of papers from the Department
                    regarding the Colorado River question, and note on page 4 of Dr. Timm’s<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d497-f1"/> memorandum of conversation dated January
                        25th<anchor n="14" xml:id="d497-f2"/> a reference to the risk we might run
                    were this matter ever submitted to international arbitration.</p>
                <p>The reference to the possibility that Mexico might make a cut just below the
                    upper boundary smacks somewhat of Federal Project No. 5 on the Rio
                        Grande.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d497-f3"/> That is to say, it would be
                    difficult for our Government to object should Mexico undertake the cut on the
                    Colorado River in Mexican territory.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d497-f1" n="13" xml:id="d497-f1-content">
                <p>Charles A. Timm, Divisional Assistant, Division of the American Republics.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f2" n="14" xml:id="d497-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f3" n="15" xml:id="d497-f3-content">
                <p>A proposed valley gravity canal and storage project for the lower Rio Grande
                    valley in Texas.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
